01:09:22,500 --> 01:09:28,500
Concrete Cowboy is a 2020 American drama film directed by Ricky
Staub from a screenplay by Staub and Dan Walser.

11
01:16:18,750 --> 01:16:24,750
Based on the novel Ghetto Cowboy by Greg Neri, it was inspired by the real urban African-American
horseriding culture of Philadelphia, specifically, the Fletcher Street Urban Riding Club.

12
01:23:15,000 --> 01:23:21,000
It stars Idris Elba, Caleb McLaughlin, Jharrel Jerome, Byron Bowers,
Lorraine Toussaint, and Clifford "Method Man" Smith.

13
01:30:11,250 --> 01:30:17,250
While the film is completely fictional, several real members of the Fletcher Street riding community
play supporting characters who give voice to real issues that the community faces.

14
01:37:07,500 --> 01:37:13,500
Concrete Cowboy had its world premiere at the Toronto International Film Festival on
September 14, 2020, and was digitally released on Netflix on April 2, 2021.

15
01:44:03,750 --> 01:44:09,750
The tone is emotional.
